# Recipient lists and anything derived from them.
#
# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC. The testnet registration form collected 3,000+ email
# addresses, and a committed export of those is a data breach that a force-push
# does not undo — the objects stay reachable, and GitHub's forks and caches keep
# their own copies. So the list never enters the tree, and the campaign tooling
# reads it from a path outside the repo.
#
# Matched by extension rather than by one expected filename, because the mistake
# this prevents is a browser download landing here under whatever name Google
# Forms chose.
*.csv
*.tsv
*.xlsx
/campaign-list*
/send-state*.json

# Cloudflare Worker local state, for the two workers in scripts/.
#
# .dev.vars is the one that matters: it is the file wrangler's own docs tell you to
# put secrets in for local runs, it is not covered by the .env* rule above, and this
# repository is public. .wrangler/ is build cache and local storage — noise at best,
# and it can contain a copy of whatever a dev run was given.
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
.wrangler/
